WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.397
This query creates pairs of customers that share the same normalized phone number.

00:00:04.397 --> 00:00:13.472
The condition a ID less than b ID avoids comparing a row with itself and avoids duplicate pair orderings.

00:00:13.472 --> 00:00:15.157
These are possible duplicates, not proven duplicates.

00:00:15.157 --> 00:00:21.507
A shared phone number may represent one person, a household, or reused contact information.

00:00:21.507 --> 00:00:27.952
Review may be necessary. Duplicate resolution requires a definition of identity and a survivor rule.

00:00:27.952 --> 00:00:32.792
Exact duplicate rows are easy; duplicate people or customers are harder.

00:00:32.792 --> 00:00:39.002
If you choose one survivor, document the priority—latest update, verified source, highest completeness,

00:00:39.002 --> 00:00:44.103
or another defensible rule—and preserve links to the merged records.
